# Fixed defect 130's class, 2026-10-01, ruling 2 of the recovery batches
# (lane recovery-b5's C5; the audit's rows 130-B2a and 130-B2b). Symptom:
# `record {` over its fields was told `expected_name`, whose words named the
# name and not where the fields go, so the braces were a second turn once
# the name was written (`expected_end_of_line` at the `{`); the same for
# `variant {`, `function {`, `constant {`, `test {`, `extern {`, a foreign
# word's `struct {`; and an `extern` group's nameless `record {` cost a
# second message, `expected_extern_signature`, at the fields it left below
# it. Cause: the report for the missing name was written for the name alone.
# Repair: where a `{` stands in the name's or the header's place, the one
# report says both, the name and where the block goes, one level deeper and
# never in braces (`parse/heads.in_braces`, `foreign_at.in_braces`); a
# group's record whose name is missing reads its fields as a top-level
# record's are, silently; and `record = {`, a map's braces where the name
# goes, is dropped whole with its line, where its `}` was refused as a
# declaration of its own (`parse/brace_habit.skip_line`).

record {  #~ expected_name
    x: i64
}

variant {  #~ expected_name
    red
}

function {  #~ expected_name
    print(1)
}

constant {  #~ expected_name
    5
}

test {  #~ expected_test_name
    assert 1 == 1
}

extern {  #~ expected_extern_header
    function abs(n: i32) -> i32
}

struct {  #~ reserved_word
    y: i64
}

record = {  #~ expected_name
    z: i64
}

extern "stdlib.h"
    record {  #~ expected_name
        quot: i32
    }

function main()
    print(1)
